$task_contents[1] = <<<'HTML'
<div class="content-block">
    <p>Every network device, from the router in a home office to the camera watching a warehouse floor, ships with a working login already installed. Manufacturers set these logins so a technician can configure the device the moment it is powered on. The problem begins when that same login is left in place long after the device goes into daily use, sitting exposed for anyone who knows where to look.</p>

    <p>By the end of this room you will be able to explain why default credentials remain such a common weakness, use a credential database to identify the factory login for a given device, and recognize how credentials leaked in unrelated data breaches end up unlocking accounts elsewhere through password reuse. A hands on simulation is included so you can practice locating and using default credentials against a small set of simulated devices.</p>

