// TASK 2: What Are Default Credentials?
$task_contents[2] = <<<'HTML'
<div class="content-block">
    <h2>A Login Nobody Changed</h2>

    <p>A <strong>default credential</strong> is a username and password that a manufacturer sets before a device ever leaves the factory. It exists so an installer can log in for the first time and finish setting the device up. That first login is meant to be temporary.</p>

    <p>In practice, it often is not. Home users plug in a router and never open the settings again. Businesses roll out dozens of identical cameras or printers and assume someone else will secure them. The factory login quietly stays active, and because the same model shares the same login everywhere, one lookup is all an attacker needs.</p>

    <div class="info-box">
        <h4><i class="fas fa-exclamation-triangle"></i> Why This Matters</h4>
        <p>Think of a default credential like a house key left under the mat by the builder. Every house built from the same plan has a mat, and every mat hides the same key. Changing the lock after moving in is the only way to make that key useless.</p>
    </div>

