// TASK 3: Using Default Credential Databases
$task_contents[3] = <<<'HTML'
<div class="content-block">
    <h2>Looking Up the Factory Login</h2>

    <p>A <strong>default credential database</strong> is a searchable reference of factory usernames and passwords, organized by device vendor and model. Security testers use these databases as a starting point when assessing a new device, because trying the known default is far faster than guessing.</p>

    <p>These databases work the same way a locksmith might keep a reference book of factory key patterns for common lock brands. Instead of picking a lock from scratch, the locksmith checks whether it matches a known pattern first.</p>

